<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Bone Sultanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1330 CE – 1905 CE (approx.) · capital Watampone</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The most powerful Bugis kingdom of South Sulawesi, whose prince Arung Palakka allied with the Dutch to break the power of Gowa in 1669.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Bone arose in the 14th century around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/watampone">Watampone</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-bone">Gulf of Bone</a>. Its chronicles tell of a tomanurung, a heavenly figure, who agreed to rule with the consent of the local community leaders. By the 16th century it was a rival of Gowa, and in 1582 it formed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tellumpoccoe">Tellumpoccoe</a> alliance with Wajo and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/soppeng-kingdom">Soppeng</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Bone was ruled by an arumpone, whose power was balanced by a council of seven lords. Gowa conquered it and imposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> in 1611. The exiled prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arung-palakka">Arung Palakka</a> joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dutch-east-india-company-territories">Dutch East India Company</a>, defeated Gowa in 1666 to 1669, and made Bone the leading state of South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulawesi">Sulawesi</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Bone resisted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> in the 19th century, and in 1905 they conquered it, exiling its ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-pawawoi-karaeng-sigeri">La Pawawoi Karaeng Sigeri</a>. The kingdom was restored under Dutch supervision in 1931 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-mappanyukki">La Mappanyukki</a> and merged into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/indonesia">Indonesia</a> after independence. It is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bone-regency">Bone Regency</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/bone-sultanate.jpg" alt="Bone Sultanate" width="320" height="290"><figcaption>Image: M.T.H. Perelaer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Bone.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1330 CE – 1905 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Watampone</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Arung Palakka, La Pawawoi Karaeng Sigeri, La Mappanyukki</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bugis</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/indonesia">Indonesia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Bone, Bone</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1618&amp;focus=bone-sultanate" aria-label="Bone Sultanate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="8017 2347 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Bone Sultanate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8337 2603L8312 2628M8337 2603L7959 2663M8337 2603L7959 2663"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8312 2628h0M7959 2663h0M7959 2663h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8337 2603h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8337 2603h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1618&amp;focus=bone-sultanate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

